    {
      "id": "method-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "data.source/source transport supplies executable source, or the node holds no source and names the import its source comes through (`data.bridgedMethod = { bridgeNodeId, key }`), in which case it runs the Method its template hands on; data.effects contains kinds update-node, create-node, delete-node, edges, emit-event and hand-off. update-node/delete-node may list targets; absent targets mean any in scope. An older allowMutations flag is read with warnings instead of pretending it was a precise declaration.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
